# Instrument 4-11 — the waystation on the north road.
#
# The four things entry 030 says a mission needs that a map deliberately cannot hold, plus the
# squads. This file replaced three copies of the same facts: a prose header in
# content/maps/waystation.hexmap, a scenario in game/scripts/SandboxScenario.cs, and a harness in
# content/Hexcom.Content.Tests/Waystation. Entry 038 said what was wrong with three; entry 047
# says what this is instead. Anything that wants to fight the waystation reads this.

mission Instrument 4-11: the waystation
map waystation

# ---- the briefing, in the mission book's six parts ------------------------------------------

brief instrument  Instrument 4-11 continues in force and this is an inspection of the waystation
brief instrument  on the north road, filed accordingly. A walk.

brief presence    A detail of four, we think, holding the crossroads. One outside the west gate
brief presence    watching the road. One on the roof of the house inside the compound, and that
brief presence    is the one with the set. A rifle in the tower to the south-east, four metres
brief presence    up, and one more in the barn on the east road. They have held this place a
brief presence    fortnight and nobody has come up the road in that time.

brief task        Enter the compound, confirm what is stored in the house, and come out.

brief restraint   You will not be seen and you will not fire. The people who live in the cottages
brief restraint   are not part of this.

brief way-off     Off by the cottages, west of the stream and north of the road, before first
brief way-off     light. Not the road you came in by: the sentry has had all night to watch it.

brief stop        If one of them properly registers you, and lives to keep it or has already
brief stop        passed it to the roof, the task is over. Come home by the cottages. There is
brief stop        nothing here worth the second half of the night.

# ---- named ground ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The way off has to be somewhere the person meeting you can find, which is why it is a place and
# not a map edge (entry 030). The two cottages share a wall and have one door, on the road side.
place cottages hexes -14,6 -14,7 -13,6

# ---- who is standing where ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Ours, on the west road about twenty hexes out, facing the crossroads. Twenty hexes is 35 m at
# the 1.73 m pitch entry 007 fixed, which is far enough out that the distances discriminate.
deploy Vance  player -21,3  facing se role scout   kit infiltrator
deploy Orsini player -20,0  facing ne role trooper kit heavy
deploy Bekker player -19,-3 facing ne              kit rifleman

# Theirs. The sentry watches the road we are coming up. The spotter has the roof and the set, and
# AwarenessTracker.CanReach gives a radio the whole side — so whatever the roof works out, the
# tower and the barn know, and neither can see that far itself. The barn and the tower are both
# outside earshot of the compound (entry 037), so if the roof goes quiet, so do they.
deploy Sentry   hostile -5,0     facing sw                 kit beamer
deploy Spotter  hostile 0,1@1    facing nw role signaller  kit beamer
deploy Watchman hostile 16,-14@1 facing nw                 kit rifleman
deploy Hollis   hostile 14,-6    facing sw                 kit beamer

# ---- what we came to do ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Suspicious is a dog barking at 25; Searching is 50, the rung where a sentry stops scanning and
# starts walking towards where he thinks you were. The brief says properly registered, so the
# threshold is the higher one and a suspicion is survivable.
objective withdrawal player exit cottages unnoticed suspicious

# Before first light. Thirty rounds covers every fight seen on this ground with room to spare —
# entry 038 measured the fighting over by round 21 — and nothing in the rules reads this yet, so
# whatever runs the battle applies it.
rounds 30
